      "side": 1,
      "message": "The difficulty with adding it to that is it requires a module to be defined in .mk and not all modules do that. e.g. if you run `m art.module.public.api` without this change it will fail because it does not define a module in .mk (no AndroidMkEntries returned) because make has no equivalent to a java_sdk_library. Other java_sdk_library modules do define an mk module by virtue of the embedded java_library but `art.module.public.api` does not build that because it is api_only.\n\nI purposely made this change here so it would work whether or not a module defined a .mk module to try and ensure consistent behaviour across all modules.",
      "parentUuid": "996d516b_8d7d8b43",
      "revId": "11a7037813e83f82f0326c370254cc24b1d292cb",
